{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 561", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320", "headline": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80"}], "files": [], "text": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(1729) = 36 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 1729 = 7 * 13 * 19; lambda is the lcm of 6 (7^1), 12 (13^1), 18 (19^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1729) = 1296\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 36\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 1729", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "1729 = 7 * 13 * 19; lambda is the lcm of 6 (7^1), 12 (13^1), 18 (19^1)", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1729) = 1296", "headline": "lambda(1729) = 36 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 36"}], "files": [], "text": "lambda(1729) = 36 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 1729 = 7 * 13 * 19; lambda is the lcm of 6 (7^1), 12 (13^1), 18 (19^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(1729) = 1296\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 36\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(9223372036854775807) = 119536704 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 9223372036854775807 = 7^2 * 73 * 127 * 337 * 92737 * 649657; lambda is the lcm of 42 (7^2), 72 (73^1), 126 (127^1), 336 (337^1), 92736 (92737^1), 649656 (649657^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(9223372036854775807) = 7713001620195508224\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 17, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 2^63-1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "9223372036854775807 = 7^2 * 73 * 127 * 337 * 92737 * 649657; lambda is the lcm of 42 (7^2), 72 (73^1), 126 (127^1), 336 (337^1), 92736 (92737^1), 649656 (649657^1)", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(9223372036854775807) = 7713001620195508224", "headline": "lambda(9223372036854775807) = 119536704 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "lambda(9223372036854775807) = 119536704 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 9223372036854775807 = 7^2 * 73 * 127 * 337 * 92737 * 649657; lambda is the lcm of 42 (7^2), 72 (73^1), 126 (127^1), 336 (337^1), 92736 (92737^1), 649656 (649657^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(9223372036854775807) = 7713001620195508224\n"}, "isError": false}}
